## what answered each survivor (commit 22942c7, then the retest in mutants-e44-retest.log)
# K4 entry bound to its sibling's record: test e4_checkpoint_refuses_an_entry_bound_to_its_siblings_record.
# K5 a stored root swapped with its summary: damage case 'two stored roots swapped with their summaries'.
# K10 the protect set: a replay-written snapshot now seals replay's protect set, which open recomputes from the journal
#     and compares; retested as K10a (compared) and K10b (restored on resume).
# K11 history durable before a replay checkpoint: a crash just after a replay checkpoint must resume from it; and every
#     restored entry must have its records in history.redb (retested as K11b).
# K12 roots record against its snapshot: (see the retest).
# K15 restored entries slimmed: test e4_checkpoint_resumes_slimmed_offloaded_and_evicting_chains; it also found a real bug,
#     restore refused a slimmed entry still holding a version (fixed in 22942c7).
# K17 eviction set restored: the same test (side cap 1 evicts).
# K18 a missing node marks the store damaged: damage case 'a missing node only the newest checkpoint names' (see the retest).
# K19 genesis's version check: removed in 22942c7. That version is the one enable_store builds from the admitted
#     genesis state at open, so the check could not fail; no mutant remains.
# K20 import sequence beyond next_seq: damage case 'a next import sequence below an entry's'.
